  "frozen_placement": "Base cache is generic support + transferred R. Only result-region keys and/or values are replaced by the fresh-R tensors computed after that same support. Support, prefix and separator tensors, token IDs, packed positions, masks, cursor, prompts and greedy decoding are identical. Keys are copied as stored; no RoPE is applied again.",
  "stats_note": "Primary comparison is the twelve-line protocol; single-label is secondary. Bootstrap resamples the nine source cases (2000 draws); labels are not independent examples. Deltas are right minus left; cases_increased / cases_decreased give direction only, so for error counts an increase is worse. Final-choice accuracy is reported separately from label accuracy.",
  "interpretation_guide": "If fresh K + transferred V substantially recovers, changing the keys is sufficient for improvement; that strengthens investigating attention or query-side adaptation while keeping transferred values. If transferred K + fresh V substantially recovers, the values deserve closer investigation, including selective reconstruction. If only replacing both works well, the key/value interaction matters and a one-component repair may be insufficient. If a hybrid works under only one prompt, the repair is sensitive to how B is asked to use the message. Mixed caches are diagnostic interventions: they do not establish that keys or values 'contain the error', and computing fresh states does not demonstrate an efficient repair. Nine cases are diagnostic examples, not independent confirmation."
}